envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-capability
type: schema
id: capability
context: >-
  emerge/schemas — sovereign local copy. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.capability (shared
  canonical version, may have moved on independently since this copy was made — sovereignty means
  emerge does not depend on it at runtime, not that the two can never drift).
intent: null
summary: null
system: emerge
tags: []
exported_at: 1789235656678
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    guardian/registry-components.js — the real _c() helper's output shape, one real object per
    registered route/capability. `intent` promoted to a required top-level field this pass, per the
    real precedent already sitting in job.dispatch's own record: `hooks.in: [{
    id:'guardian.job.dispatch.receive', intent:['build','ask','forge','compile'], ... }]` — that
    array already exists in real code, just nested and optional (hooks defaults to {}). No other
    real capability record in registry-components.js currently sets it, so most existing rows would
    need a real intent list backfilled to satisfy this as REQUIRED, not just a schema-level promise.
  fields:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, namespaced id — '<namespace>.<name>', e.g. 'guardian.health'
    namespace:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real system namespace, e.g. 'guardian'
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real capability name within the namespace
    version:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real version string, e.g. '3.6.2' — sourced from the file's own version const
    grammar:
      type: array
      required: true
      description: >-
        real natural-language trigger phrases for this capability, defaults to [name-with-spaces,
        name-with-dashes] if not given explicitly
    route:
      type: object
      required: true
      description: >-
        real {method, path} — the actual HTTP route this capability maps to. This IS the
        capability→.command link: identical shape to schema.command's own {method, path}, always
        present, so "maps to at least one .command" already holds structurally for every real row.
    intent:
      type: array
      required: true
      description: >-
        real intent-verb list this capability serves, e.g. ['build','ask','forge','compile'] — the
        capability→.intent link. Promoted from job.dispatch's own real (but optional, nested)
        hooks.in[].intent to a required top-level field, per this pass's own instruction.
        checkPayload only checks presence + typeof here, NOT non-empty — see §KNOWN GAP below.
    description:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, human-readable description of what this capability does
    params:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: real declared parameters, defaults to []
    tags:
      type: array
      required: true
      description: real tags, always includes the namespace itself plus any caller-supplied tags
    permissions:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: real required permissions, defaults to ['system']
    hooks:
      type: object
      required: false
      description: >-
        real associated hook references, defaults to {} — the original, nested home of intent[],
        kept for backward compatibility
    events:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: >-
        §NOT GROUNDED — no real capability record anywhere in the codebase currently declares which
        .event(s) it emits. Left optional and unenforced deliberately: marking this required would
        mean inventing a shape with no real construction site to check it against, which breaks this
        registry's own grounding rule. A real per-capability event-emission list (e.g. registry-
        components.js's _c() gaining an `events:` opt, mirroring how `hooks.in[].intent` already
        works) would need to exist in real code before this can honestly be REQUIRED.
